---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'China Visa Types Complete Guide 2026: Which Visa Do You Need?';
const description = 'A complete guide to Chinese visa types for tourists in 2026: visa-free, mutual agreements, 240-hour transit, and L-type tourist visa.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/en/visa/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Prepare
      </a>
    </nav>
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">📋 Entry & Visa</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        China Visa Types Complete Guide 2026: Which Visa Do You Need?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Getting into China is easier than it was a few years ago. Here's what you need to know.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Answer Box -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-4">🎯 Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-blue-800 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Whether you need a visa depends on your passport.</strong> Citizens of 50 countries can enter visa-free for up to 30 days, and another 29 have mutual visa-free agreements. Travelers from 55 countries can use the 240-hour transit policy. Everyone else needs a standard L-type Tourist Visa.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#need-visa" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🛂 Do You Need a Visa to Visit China?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how-long" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">⏱️ How Long Does It Take?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#mutual" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🤝 Mutual Visa-Free Agreements</a></li>
        <li><a href="#which-option" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🤔 Which Option Is Right for You?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#faq" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">❓ Frequently Asked Questions</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <strong>Getting into China is easier than it was a few years ago.</strong>
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Depending on your nationality and travel plans, you might be able to enter China without a visa, take advantage of the 240-hour transit policy, or apply for a standard tourist visa. For most travelers, the process is straightforward once you figure out which option applies to your situation.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 id="need-visa" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🛂</span> Do You Need a Visa to Visit China?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <strong>Not everyone needs a traditional Chinese visa.</strong> There are currently three common ways to enter China:
      </p>

      <!-- Section 1: Visa-Free -->
      <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-green-200 text-green-800 text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Visa-Free Entry</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          China currently grants visa-free entry to citizens of 50 countries (plus 29 mutual agreement countries) for stays of up to 30 days. If your passport is from one of these countries, you can literally book a flight and walk through Chinese immigration without having applied for anything in advance. Just make sure your passport is valid for at least 6 months beyond your entry date, and you're good to go.
        </p>
        <a href="/en/visa/visa-free/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium hover:underline">
          China Visa-Free Countries List (2026) →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 2: 240-Hour Transit -->
      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-200 text-blue-800 text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">240-Hour Visa-Free Transit</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Travelers from eligible countries can stay in China for up to 240 hours (10 days) while transiting to a third country or region (including Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan).
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          This option is popular with travelers making stopovers in cities like Shanghai, Beijing, Guangzhou, and Chengdu. <strong>Important note:</strong> This policy only applies to entries through international airports, not land border crossings.
        </p>
        <a href="/en/visa/transit-240/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium hover:underline">
          China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Explained →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 3: Mutual Agreement -->
      <div class="bg-teal-50 border border-teal-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-teal-200 text-teal-800 text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Mutual Visa-Free Agreements</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          In addition to China's unilateral visa-free policy, China has signed <strong>mutual visa-exemption agreements</strong> with <strong>29 countries</strong>. Citizens of these countries holding ordinary passports can enter China visa-free.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Stay duration varies by agreement — many allow up to <strong>30 days</strong> per entry, while some (like Singapore) permit stays of up to <strong>90 days within any 180-day period</strong>. Always check the specific terms of your country's agreement before traveling.
        </p>
        <a href="/en/visa/mutual-agreement/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium hover:underline">
          Mutual Visa-Free Agreements (29 Countries) →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 4: Tourist Visa -->
      <div class="bg-purple-50 border border-purple-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-purple-200 text-purple-800 text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Tourist Visa (L-type)</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If neither of the options above works for you, you'll typically need a Chinese L-type Tourist Visa.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The application process is generally straightforward and requires:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-gray-700 mb-4">
          <li>A valid passport</li>
          <li>A completed application form</li>
          <li>A recent photo</li>
          <li>Supporting documents (as required)</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/en/visa/apply-l-visa/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium hover:underline">
          How to Apply for China Tourist Visa (L-Type) →
        </a>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 id="how-long" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">⏱️</span> How Long Does It Take?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Processing times vary by country and visa center. In most locations, standard processing takes 4–5 business days, though faster expedited services may be available for an additional fee.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 id="which-option" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🤔</span> Which Option Is Right for You?
      </h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-12 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
          <caption class="text-sm text-gray-500 italic mb-2">China visa types overview for foreign travelers</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-900 text-white">
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold"></th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold text-center bg-green-600">30-Day Visa-Free</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold text-center bg-teal-600">Mutual Agreement</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold text-center bg-blue-600">240-Hour Transit</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold text-center bg-purple-600">L Tourist Visa</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Who qualifies</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">50 countries</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">29 countries</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">55 countries</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Everyone else</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Max stay</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">30 days</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">30–90 days (varies)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">10 days (240 hours)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">30–90 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Advance paperwork</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">None</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">None</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">None (just show up)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">4–5 business days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Cost</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Free</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Free</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Free</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">$30–$100 USD</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Flexibility</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Travel anywhere</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Travel anywhere</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Region-restricted</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 text-center">Travel anywhere</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

    <!-- FAQPage Schema -->
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is visa-free entry the same as a visa?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Visa-free entry means you don't need a visa stamp in your passport at all. You just show your passport to immigration and they let you in. It's completely different from having a visa \u2014 it's the absence of one."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need to register with police after entering visa-free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If you're staying at a hotel, they'll handle the registration automatically. If you're staying at a private residence, your host needs to register you at the local police station within 24 hours. This applies regardless of how you entered China."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What if I have dual citizenship?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "China doesn't recognize dual nationality. Use the passport you intend to enter China with. If one of your passports is from a visa-free country, use that one \u2014 it simplifies everything."
          }
        }
      ]
    })}></script>

      <h2 id="faq" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">❓</span> Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-6 mb-8">
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is visa-free entry the same as a visa?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>No.</strong> Visa-free entry means you don't need a visa stamp in your passport at all. You just show your passport to immigration and they let you in. It's completely different from having a visa — it's the absence of one.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I need to register with police after entering visa-free?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If you're staying at a hotel, they'll handle the registration automatically. If you're staying at a private residence, your host needs to register you at the local police station within 24 hours. This applies regardless of how you entered China.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">What if I have dual citizenship?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">China doesn't recognize dual nationality. Use the passport you intend to enter China with. If one of your passports is from a visa-free country, use that one — it simplifies everything.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Before applying for a visa, check whether you qualify for visa-free entry or the 240-hour transit policy. If not, a standard L-type Tourist Visa remains the most common route for visitors.
      </p>
    </div>

